<p>Select the collate type applied when the collate function is selected.</p>
<p>Note that the collate types that are available will vary depending 
 on your printer or the configuration.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="type" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Collate Type:</span></p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Collate</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Print sets are all delivered in the same orientation. 
 </p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Rotating Collate</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Every other print set is rotated by 90 degrees and 
 delivered to the output tray. <span class="Term-Soft">Rotating Collate</span> 
 is available only if paper of the same size is loaded in <img alt="" class="help-icon" height="12" loading="lazy" src="~/images/help/BPortMin.gif" width="12"/> <img alt="" class="help-icon" height="12" loading="lazy" src="~/images/help/BLandMin.gif" width="12"/> in the trays (in portrait or landscape orientation).</p>
<p class="Note-indent">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">If you specify 
 a tray other than <span class="Term-Soft">Auto Tray Select</span> for the 
 input tray, <span class="Term-Soft">Rotating Collate</span> is not available.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Shift Collate</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Print sets are alternately shifted when delivered 
 to the output tray. Stapled print sets are not shifted.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ok" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">OK</span></p>
<p>Saves the changes and closes the dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cancel" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Cancel</span></p>
<p>Closes the dialog box without saving any changes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="help" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Help</span></p>
<p>Displays Help for the dialog box opened.</p>
